rem Sum of Largest Prime Factors
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=642

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

arg N integer = 201820182018

rem With F(v, q) the sum of the largest
rem prime factors of numbers up to v
rem whose primes beyond q are used
rem last, F(v, q) = G(v) - G(q) + sum
rem over primes p > q, p^2 <= v, and
rem e >= 1 with p^(e + 1) <= v of F(v
rem // p^e, p) + p, G the prime sum.
rem Writing C(v) = G(v) + the rest,
rem each prime p, taken from the largest
rem down, adds C(v // p^e) - G(p - 1)
rem to C(v) for every v >= p^(e + 1),
rem over all v = N // k (a table for
rem the small ones). G comes from a
rem Lucy sieve mod 10^9; the answer is
rem C(N).
M = 1000000000
R = N isqrt
Vs = 0 to R
Ev = Vs + (Vs mod 2)
Od = Vs + 1 - (Vs mod 2)
Hv = (Ev // 2) mod M * (Od mod M)
Gs = Hv mod M - 1
Gs 0 = 0
Wl = N // (Vs max 1)
El = Wl + (Wl mod 2)
Ol = Wl + 1 - (Wl mod 2)
Hw = (El // 2) mod M * (Ol mod M)
Gl = Hw mod M - 1
Pr = primes to R array
for P in Pr
  Gp = Gs (P - 1)
  Ih = R min (N // (P * P))
  Ix = 1 to Ih
  Pi = P * Ix
  Mk = Pi at most R
  Va = Gl (Pi min R)
  Vb = Gs ((N // Pi) min R)
  Dv = (Mk choose Va Vb) - Gp
  Gl Ix = (Gl Ix - P * Dv) mod M
  Iw = P * P to R
  Qd = Gs (Iw // P) - Gp
  Gs Iw = (Gs Iw - P * Qd) mod M
end
Cs = Gs copy
Cl = Gl copy
Gf = Gs copy
for P in Pr reverse
  Gv = Gf (P - 1)
  Ih = R min (N // (P * P))
  Is = 1 to Ih
  Al = Is * 0
  Sw = P * P
  Sv = Sw to R
  As = (Sv * 0)
  Pe = P
  for Pe * P at most N
    Ie = R min (N // (Pe * P))
    Ix = 1 to Ie
    Pi = Pe * Ix
    Mk = Pi at most R
    Va = Cl (Pi min R)
    Vb = Cs ((N // Pi) min R)
    Dv = (Mk choose Va Vb) - Gv
    Al (Ix - 1) += Dv
    if Pe * P at most R
      Sx = Pe * P to R
      Ds = (Cs (Sx // Pe)) - Gv
      As (Sx - Sw) += Ds
    end
    Pe *= P
  end
  Cl Is = (Cl Is + Al) mod M
  if Sw at most R
    Cs Sv = (Cs Sv + As) mod M
  end
end
Answer = Cl 1 mod M
Answer print
